# TestKotlinVsJavaFernflower: fernflower's main set analysed twice, as Java and as its J2K translation to Kotlin
# (maddi-run-analysis's j2k/fernflower-nullability output), with the same configuration otherwise. Two-sided, as
# CensusRatchet: a line that is new fails (a regression, or a change to record deliberately), and a recorded line that
# is gone fails too (an improvement: remove it in the commit that earns it). The test writes the actual lines to
# build/kotlin-vs-java/fernflower/fernflower.ratchet.actual.
#
# Recorded: the per-side numbers, each kind's summary (the naming categories, accessors, companions, ..., by count
# only), then every element of a category that judges a verdict: kotlin-weaker (precision the Kotlin side lost),
# kotlin-stronger (Kotlin claims more than Java: a soundness question, maddi-mod#145), kotlin-none/java-none,
# differ (types), java-only and kotlin-only-other. A verdict is true for unmodified (F, P) or non-modifying (M).
#
# 2026-11-19, first record: maddi a2cc271ff (with the forEach lowering, 92e523553 + d81b290e3), maddi-mod f3531e77,
# run on the Mac. Known: appendTypeParameters#3 kotlin-weaker is a Java gap (maddi-mod#138); the ConstExprent maps and
# ClassWriter.MODIFIERS kotlin-stronger are Java counting its static initializer as a modification.

